  "answer": "Citation complaints changed from a sharp Q1 increase to a steady Q2 decline. In Q1, a review of 210 accuracy-related tickets found complaints about incorrect file links (42%), missing page numbers (28%), empty citations (18%), and broken links (12%) [NL-010#NL-010-S05]. After the April product release, citation accuracy tickets fell from 88 in March to 42 in April, then 31 in May and 24 in June [NL-011#NL-011-S05]. Q2 reporting describes this as a significant decrease in citation-related complaints, with remaining May/June citation tickets almost entirely linked to scanned, image-only PDFs where TutorChat cannot establish page-level citation anchors [NL-011#NL-011-S05] [NL-016#NL-016-S04].\n\nThe planned product work that directly addresses the remaining scanned-document problem is the Advanced OCR Pipeline. The Q1 action items call for implementing an integrated OCR pipeline to address scanned PDF challenges, with an OCR pilot targeted for August 2026 [NL-010#NL-010-S10]. This is confirmed as an Active Advanced OCR Pipeline scheduled for release in August 2026 that will automatically extract text and layout structures from scanned files, enabling page-specific citations [NL-024#NL-024-S04].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
